# Context budget
- `index.html` is ~850 KB (~210k tokens). Never read it whole and never open line 1369 (one 12 KB data line). Use `docs/code-map.md` (line numbers of sections, CSS blocks, constants, functions) or `grep -n`, then read at most ~150 lines around the target. Run `python3 tools/dev/code_map.py` after editing index.html.
- `CLAUDE.md` (~45 KB) is the full project notes. Don't read it top to bottom: `grep -n` it for the feature or function you touch and read those bullets only.
- Never read `data/libraries/*.json`, `media/`, `node_modules/`, `cdk.out/`, or lock files. Read `docs/dev-log.md` only from the tail (last ~40 lines).
- Prefer small, targeted edits over rewriting large blocks. One feature per session.

# Hard rules
- Work only on branch `cursor-dev`. Never checkout, merge into or push `main` (it deploys co2trace.io). No force-push, no deploys, no paid cloud actions, no secrets in the repo.
- After editing any inline `<script>` in index.html: `python3 tools/security/csp.py`, then `--check` must pass. Escape user values with `esc()`; no inline event handlers, no `eval`.
- Keep English and Spanish in step (`data-es`, `L(en, es)`). Examples stay fixed and fictional; no new edit paths into examples.
- Cite ISO standards only by number and clause; never paste standard text.
- Record what you build as a short dated bullet in `CLAUDE.md` (same terse style).

# Major changes need Jorge's approval
A change is MAJOR if it does any of: changes calculation results, emission factors, GWPs, country rules or example figures; removes or rewrites an existing feature, section or report; redesigns look, layout, branding or navigation; changes the saved data format (`state` shape/version, localStorage/IndexedDB keys); touches `api/`, `infra/`, `co2trace.config.js`, `CNAME`, auth, billing, plans or prices; adds a dependency, outside host (CSP `BASE`) or paid/cloud service; changes legal, compliance or regulatory wording; or is likely to change more than ~300 lines.
- Never build a major change unless `.dev/approvals.txt` has `approve <id>` for its proposal. Instead write a proposal in `docs/proposals.md` (`## P-YYYYMMDD-n: title`, what, why, what Jorge will see, risk, size, alternatives), mark the backlog item `AWAITING APPROVAL (P-…)`, and work on a minor item.
- `reject <id>: reason` in `.dev/approvals.txt` means drop or rework the item as the reason says.
- If a minor item turns out major while building, stop, revert your uncommitted edits, and propose it.
